      \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\sl286 \fs22\lang1033\f0 The compiler may infer caller lifetime for values in return position when the return type specifies it.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_types_45_lifetime_45_thrown}{\*\bkmkend ID_types_45_lifetime_45_thrown}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 4.13.5 Thrown Lifetime (!)\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Error values use thrown lifetime. The value is allocated on a special exception page provided by the caller:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\sl257 \fs19\lang1024\f2 \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
