the resulting string.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 "hello"\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 hello \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 ""\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2  \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_CHARACTER_45_LITERALS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_CHARACTER_45_LITERALS}\b\fs28\f1 7.2.6 Character Literals\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Character literals represent a single character, enclosed in backticks.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 `a`\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 a \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 `Z`\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 Z \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s2\sl413 {\*\bkmkstart ID_category_45_OPERATIONS}{\*\bkmkend ID_category_45_OPERATIONS}\b\fs31\f1 7.3 Operations\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Operations allow combining expressions.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_PREFIX_45_FUNCTIONS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_PREFIX_45_FUNCTIONS}\b\fs28\lang1024\f1 7.3.1 Prefix Functions\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 An operation is a sequence of operands that evaluates to a single value. Each operand is an expression optionally followed by member access. An operation ends with a colon, a line break, or anything which is not an expression. Evaluation uses a context which is empty at the start of an operation. When the context is empty, operator-shaped identifiers act as prefix functions, taking the next operand as their argument.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -(-3)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 + 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_OPERATOR_45_CHAINS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_OPERATOR_45_CHAINS}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.2 Operator Chains\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 When the context holds a value, operators combine with operands according to standard mathematical precedence. Multiplicative operators (*, /, %, div, mod) bind tighter than additive operators (+, -). Comparison and equality operators have lower precedence than arithmetic. Operators of equal precedence associate left-to-right.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 + 4\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 10 - 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 7 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 6 * 7\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 84 / 2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 42 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 17 % 5\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 + 4 * 2\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 11 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 20 - 5 - 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 12 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_PARENTHESES_45_GROUPING}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_PARENTHESES_45_GROUPING}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.3 Parentheses and Grouping\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Parentheses create a empty context. This allows prefix forms inside an otherwise operator chain, and explicit grouping when needed.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 * (- 2)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 -10 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 2 * (3 + 4)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 14 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 (2 + 3) * (4 + 1)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 25 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_IDENTIFIER_45_SHAPES}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_IDENTIFIER_45_SHAPES}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.4 Identifier Shapes\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Identifiers can have name shape (alphanumeric) or operator shape (symbols). The shape is purely lexical and does not determine behavior. Whether an identifier acts as a prefix function or chain operator depends on its declaration and the register state.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 10 div 3\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 3 \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\cellx4320\clvertalt\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 abs (- 5)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \fs22\f2 5 \sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\s3\sl365 {\*\bkmkstart ID_tests_45_LET_45_BINDINGS}{\*\bkmkend ID_tests_45_LET_45_BINDINGS}\b\fs28\f1 7.3.5 Let Bindings\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 \b0\fs22\lang1033\f0 Let bindings introduce local variables. The syntax is let followed by a name and a value expression (no equals sign). Multiple statements are separated by colons or newlines.\sa330\par\trowd\trql\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Input\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl286 \b\fs22\f1 Result\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trql \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx4320\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx8640 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl257 \fs19\f2 let x 5\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
