brew install llvm@18 cmake openjade\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
; Ubuntu 24.04\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
sudo apt install llvm-18-dev clang-18 cmake openjade zlib1g-dev libzstd-dev\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb330\sl286 \b\fs22\lang1033\f0 ./build.sh\b0  builds the C++ stage-0 compiler, and \f2 tools/seed.sh\f0  then bootstraps it into the self-hosted compiler and emits a fresh, fixed-point-verified seed. See \f2 RELEASING.md\f0  for the full seed-distribution process.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb165\sl286 The C++ implementation is kept buildable on purpose: it is an independent compiler lineage, which preserves a diverse-double-compiling check against trusting-trust attacks, and it is the per-platform bootstrap root for new architectures. It is not part of the language or its everyday toolchain.\hyphpar0\par}
